\chapter{Memory: Page Tables, Copy-on-Write and Swapping}
\label{ch:memory}

The x86 version of the book uses two-level page tables and a frame table. AArch64 uses four levels, address space identifiers
(ASIDs) instead of flushing the TLB, and a kernel that lives in the upper half of the address space. On top of this the port
implements \texttt{fork} with copy-on-write (a software bit in the page table entry and a reference count for each frame) and
the swapping of the book (\texttt{page\_out}, \texttt{page\_in}, the swapper process).

@
\section{Page table entry bits (4 KByte granule), shared by all ARM64 sources}
\label{src:arch_pte.h}


@

The complete file is put together from these parts:

<<arch_pte.h>>=
<<arch_pte.h: ARCH_PTE_H>>
@

<<arch_pte.h: ARCH_PTE_H>>=
#ifndef ARCH_PTE_H
#define ARCH_PTE_H
#ifndef ULIX_H
typedef unsigned long u64;
#endif

// page table entry bits (4 KB granule)
#define PTE_VALID   0x1UL
#define PTE_TABLE   0x3UL
#define PTE_PAGE    0x3UL                   // level 3: bits[1:0] = 11
#define PTE_ATTR(n) ((u64)(n) @<< 2)         // MAIR index: 0 = device, 1 = normal
#define PTE_AP_USER (1UL @<< 6)              // AP[1]: accessible from EL0
#define PTE_RO      (1UL @<< 7)              // AP[2]: read-only
#define PTE_SH      (3UL @<< 8)
#define PTE_AF      (1UL @<< 10)
#define PTE_NG      (1UL @<< 11)             // not global: the TLB entry is tagged with the ASID (user pages only)
#define PTE_PXN     (1UL @<< 53)
#define PTE_UXN     (1UL @<< 54)
#define PTE_COW     (1UL @<< 55)             // software bit (ignored by the hardware): copy-on-write page
#define PTE_SWAPPED (1UL @<< 56)             // software bit: the page is in the swap file (valid bit clear)
#define PTE_ADDR    0x0000FFFFFFFFF000UL

#define PAGE_RW     (PTE_PAGE | PTE_ATTR (1) | PTE_SH | PTE_AF | PTE_PXN | PTE_UXN)
#define PAGE_RO     (PAGE_RW | PTE_RO)
#define PAGE_URX    (PTE_NG | PTE_PAGE | PTE_ATTR (1) | PTE_SH | PTE_AF | PTE_AP_USER | PTE_RO | PTE_PXN)
#define PAGE_URO    (PTE_NG | PTE_PAGE | PTE_ATTR (1) | PTE_SH | PTE_AF | PTE_AP_USER | PTE_RO | PTE_PXN | PTE_UXN)
#define PAGE_URW    (PTE_NG | PTE_PAGE | PTE_ATTR (1) | PTE_SH | PTE_AF | PTE_AP_USER | PTE_PXN | PTE_UXN)


#endif

